{%- comment -%}
  Static page (About, FAQ, Track Your Order, the legal pages …). Display-L title
  over one narrow prose column — the legal + trust layer is the only long-form
  reading in this store, so nothing competes with it.

  NOT the shop policies: /policies/* is rendered by Shopify's own markup
  (.shopify-policy__container > .rte) and ignores any theme template for that
  route — those are styled in theme.css instead, otherwise they ship as an
  unstyled wall of text. The `policy` fallback below costs nothing and keeps
  this section correct if that route is ever templatable.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign doc = page
  if policy != blank
    assign doc = policy
  endif

  comment
    Duplicate-title strip: a page like /pages/about-us can open its own body
    with "About us" again, so the page prints the same words twice — once as
    this template's h1, once as the content's first heading. If the FIRST
    element of the body is an h1/h2/h3 whose text equals the page title, it
    is dropped. Anything else is left exactly as the merchant wrote it;
    editing the page copy stays a merchant job, this only removes a provable
    repeat.
  endcomment
  assign body = doc.content
  assign heading_tags = 'h1,h2,h3' | split: ','
-%}
{%- for tag in heading_tags -%}
  {%- assign close = '</' | append: tag | append: '>' -%}
  {%- assign chunks = body | split: close -%}
  {%- if chunks.size > 1 -%}
    {%- assign lead = chunks[0] -%}
    {%- assign lead_open = lead | strip | slice: 0, 3 -%}
    {%- assign lead_txt = lead | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- assign want_open = '<' | append: tag -%}
    {%- if lead_open == want_open and lead_txt == doc.title -%}
      {%- assign body = body | remove_first: lead | remove_first: close -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
<section class="sec--tight">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow page-head">
    <h1 class="dl">{{ doc.title | escape }}</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow page-body">
    <div class="prose">{{ body }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{ "name": "Page", "settings": [] }
{% endschema %}
